+# Independent cold review of root's sharper local-probe bound
+
+PASS for ROOT_DERIVATION.md SHA256897efdbc95fc671ea83401bae93cb2776fa5bafa5435f95d0bee43d8bb247769 in /private/tmp/toe-campaign-20260907/local-observable-cutoff/. My separate proof1244c9eb and its original freeze remain unchanged. I read root's full proof only after that freeze. Root supplied the initial incidence candidate and later sharper tail/normalization candidates before this review, as disclosed in both prospective records. No root checker was rerun and no source was edited.
+
+The model and domain agree with the explicit full-link compact Hamiltonian. The relevant primary strong-topology treatment was directly inspected in [Nachtergaele–Sims1410.8174](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1410.8174), Proposition2.1, Lemma2.2 and Theorem3.1 equations71–73. Bounded, strongly continuous interaction-picture terms have the requisite strong integrals. Uniform norm continuity or differentiability of arbitrary bounded A under the unbounded onsite generator is not assumed. The recurrence in the root proof is valid for the bounded time-dependent interaction picture: split the Jacobi identity into selfadjoint commutator evolution and forcing, then take the supremum over local A. Endpoint onsite conjugations preserve support and norm. This also handles the two-time propagation required in boundary Duhamel.
+
+I independently count first-face choices<=4|X|, subsequent choices<=16, each norm<=v. The coefficient for n>=1 is therefore <=(|X|/4)(32vT)^n/n! before the common prefactor2||A||||B||. Root's replacement by |X| is conservative. A chain of n face cliques connects its endpoints in at most n link steps, so only n>=d contribute. For d0 the initial commutator is covered because |X|>=1. Thus the stated2||A||||B||||X|Theta_d bound is safe. The exponential tail follows from1_(n>=d)<=exp(n-d), including z0 and d0 conventions.
+
+For a crossing face every link has distance>=r because one outside link has distance>=r+1 and its face has diameter1. Counting C<=4N and integrating the nonnegative series yields
+ 2v C integral_0^T Theta_r(32vs)ds = (C/16)Theta_(r+1)(32vT)
+ <=(N/4)Theta_(r+1)(32vT).
+Hence the coefficient1/4 and indexr+1 in(S) are correct. At v0 the exact integral and tail both vanish; the relaxed exponential need not, as disclosed. The cubic ball bound is polynomial and gives genuine radius convergence for fixed time. Exterior correlations are irrelevant to the exact reduced-state identity under decoupled dynamics.
+
+For(C), let chi be the unnormalized finite evolved purification, with normsqrt(p). The difference of pure rank-one operators is bounded in trace norm by (1+sqrt(p))||psi-chi||<=2||psi-chi||. Normalizing chi adds trace norm exactly1-p between its unnormalized and normalized projectors; the corresponding observable contribution is <=||A||(1-p). This proves the stronger normalization term without confusing vector and expectation errors. Partial trace handles arbitrary reference dimension. Form-energy conservation, K>=gQ and bounded PVQ justify the projected equation by form-domain approximation. No projected-input energy divided by p is needed, because the comparison evolves the original unnormalized projection. A positive preparation probability is guaranteed only when E<g, or otherwise assumed separately.
+
+The Wilson-loop adverse example is exact. Let V=U2 U3^-1 U4^-1. The product of three independent Haar variables is Haar. Both families sqrt3 U1_ab and sqrt3 V_ba are orthonormal in their respective factor spaces, by fundamental matrix-coefficient orthogonality. Expanding Tr(U1 V) gives nine coefficients1/3 and hence norm1. The single-link density has nine eigenvalues1/9 in the fundamental matrix-coefficient block and zero constant component. Its left/right gauge conjugation invariance does not make its support singlet. A zero-boundary-charge projection therefore has success probability0 on this valid global physical loop state. No Gaussian approximation or hidden gauge fixing is involved.
+
+No mathematical correction was found. The theorem concerns local expectation values with finite local energy and explicit conditioned preparation. It does not give a full-volume state estimate, uniform all-energy channel norm, native compiler, or selected physical dynamics. The extra boundary-flux clarification is load bearing and must survive canonical packaging.
