+For arbitrary local density rho_Omega with energyE_Omega under positive H_Omega, P_R cutoff gives p=tr(P rho)>=1-E/g. Purification yields unnormalizedexpectationerror<=2||A||(1+M T)sqrt(E/g); normalizing P rho P/p adds at most||A||(1-p), not an unstated freeencoder. This suggests fullerror <=spatialtail+||A||[2(1+M T)sqrt(E/g)+E/g] forp>0, with E/g<1 sufficient. Statepreparation cost and suppliedlocalenergy remainexplicit.
+
+Critical boundarydomain control: reducing a globally Gauss-singlet state to a finite spatial region need not give a state supported on the region's zero-charge singlet sector. It is gauge-invariant as a density but may carry boundary flux. Use the full finite link tensor carrier (or onlyinterior constraints), preserveboundarysectors, and never silentlyprojectlocalboundaryGauss. Seek an actual Wilson-loop cut adverseexample. No infinite-energy all-input norm/diamond claim, no physicalclock selection, no fullhardwarecompiler.
