+PASS for DERIVATION.md SHA1244c9ebbe748387b0ab8784efc82db9aebbb0655a3475ddc2d393f5734957c5. Root independently derived a parallel bound before reading this proof, with candidate/exchanged refinement timing recorded in root preregistration. The primary paper arXiv1410.8174 Proposition2.1, Lemma2.2 and equations71–73 was directly inspected; its strong-topology distinction is important and accurately preserved.
+
+The first-face4|X| and subsequent-face16 counts, factorial time ordering and minimum chain length imply the stated conservative32e propagation coefficient. The crossing-face distance is at least ell even with the neighborhood intersected with an arbitrary ambient link set. The geometric polynomial bound, C<=4N and F<=N are valid cubic incidence estimates and independent of ambient volume. The bounded boundary perturbation and strong Duhamel argument avoid an unjustified unbounded commutator with an arbitrary observable.
+
+The local reduced state carries all exterior correlations exactly for the decoupled evolution. The finite form-energy assumption permits purification and spectral approximation; P K Q=0 isolates bounded forcing and gives the stated vector error. Normalization adds1-sqrt(p), success probability is retained, and the final cap2 applies to normalized expectations. No energy guarantee is inferred when E>=g unless p is independently known positive. The projection preserves boundary representation sectors rather than imposing false local zero-charge singlets.
+
+The result correctly applies to supplied arbitrary finite v>=0, with increasing spatial resources, independently of the small-coupling gap theorem. The optional infinite-volume dynamics conclusion is a norm-Cauchy local-observable limit; it does not assert norm continuity in time on all unbounded onsite observables or normality of arbitrary states. No whole-volume state, all-input diamond or native compiler claim is present. No correction requested. Root's independently derived integrated-tail/normalization refinements are separately reviewable and are not retrospectively attributed to this frozen proof.
